steps.body:
A **sealed** type lists exactly which classes may extend or implement it:

```java
sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Square {}
record Circle(double r) implements Shape {}
record Square(double side) implements Shape {}
```

Each permitted subclass must be `final`, `sealed` or `non-sealed` (records are automatically final). Now the compiler *knows* every possible `Shape` — which pays off with pattern matching in Java 21.

Java 17 (LTS) also **strongly encapsulated JDK internals** (old libraries poking at `sun.*` classes may break), and previewed pattern matching for `switch`. Smaller additions on the way: `Collectors.teeing` and `String.indent`/`transform` (12), hidden classes (15).

Switch can now match on **types**, and **record patterns** take records apart:

```java
sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Square {}
record Circle(double r) implements Shape {}
record Square(double side) implements Shape {}

static double area(Shape s) {
    return switch (s) {
        case Circle(double r) -> Math.PI * r * r;
        case Square(double side) -> side * side;
    };
}
```

No `default` needed: `Shape` is sealed, so the compiler knows both cases are covered. Add a new `Shape` and this switch stops compiling until you handle it. Add conditions with guards: `case Circle c when c.r() > 10 -> ...`.

**Virtual threads** are lightweight threads managed by the JVM. You can run millions of blocking tasks with plain, readable code:

```java
try (var executor = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {
    executor.submit(() -> handle(request));
}
```

(More in the Concurrency unit.)

**Sequenced collections** give ordered collections one shared API: `getFirst()`, `getLast()`, `addFirst()`, `addLast()`, `reversed()` on `List`, `Deque`, `LinkedHashSet` and friends — no more `list.get(list.size() - 1)`.

Java 21 also added a generational mode for the low-pause ZGC garbage collector.

